\centering
\fbox{\begin{minipage}{0.92\linewidth}
\centering
Composition check $\rightarrow$ controlled equilibration/quench $\rightarrow$ XRD plus EPMA $\rightarrow$ microscopy/spectroscopy $\rightarrow$ compare with binary/ternary constraints $\rightarrow$ classify equilibrium or metastable product
\end{minipage}}
\caption{Phase-purity decision path used throughout the review. Each step is a measurement or comparison requirement; the sequence is not an executable synthesis protocol.}
\label{fig:decision}
\end{figure}
\section{Phase Diagrams and Thermodynamics}\label{sec:thermo}

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Thermodynamic evidence that bounds, but does not replace, a BaO--Y$_2$O$_3$--ZnO--SiO$_2$ assessment.}
\label{tab:thermo}
\begin{tabular}{P{0.22\linewidth}P{0.29\linewidth}P{0.35\linewidth}P{0.08\linewidth}}
\toprule
Subsystem & Measurement or model & Transferable constraint & Status \\
\midrule
BaO--SiO$_2$ & Binary thermodynamic and phase-equilibrium studies & Ba-rich silicate compounds and liquidus trends constrain Ba loss and melt formation & Measured neighbor \cite{shukla2018thermodynamic,zhang2016thermodynamic,tyurnina2008thermodynamic} \\
Y$_2$O$_3$--SiO$_2$ & Experimental assessments and re-optimization & Y--Si--O phase fields and uncertainties delimit possible Y silicates & Measured neighbor \cite{makrovets2023y2o3,zhi2022thermodynamic,qi2024thermodynamic} \\
ZnO--SiO$_2$ & Equilibration, liquidus, and CALPHAD studies & Zn-bearing silicate fields and solid-solution ranges constrain competing products & Measured neighbor \cite{shevchenko2019thermodynamic,jeon2025phase,dobrynenko2025solid} \\
Multicomponent oxides & Database and model architecture & Assessed Gibbs-energy functions provide a framework for a future quaternary database & Method \cite{decterov2018thermodynamic,bale2008factsage,sundman2018a} \\
Ba--Y oxide boundaries & Non-silicate phase diagrams & Invariant-reaction reasoning is transferable; phase identities are not & Boundary only \cite{kale1989phase,bryuzgina2022actual} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The BaO--SiO$_2$ and Y$_2$O$_3$--SiO$_2$ binaries establish the two network-forming edges, while ZnO--SiO$_2$ constrains zincosilicate competition. Recent ZnO-bearing assessments demonstrate the value of combining key phase-diagram experiments, rapid quenching, EPMA, and thermodynamic optimization \cite{kim2025key,abdeyazdan2024phase,jeon2025phase,lee2025coupled}. The same protocol is appropriate for selected BaO--Y$_2$O$_3$--ZnO--SiO$_2$ sections, especially those crossing the nominal target composition.

ZnO volatility and interfacial reactions are likely to matter because liquidus topology and open processing boundaries can shift the effective composition. Ba--Zn silicate glass studies and noble-metal nucleation work show that melt structure and crucible interfaces alter crystallization behavior \cite{moulton2021a,thieme2022noble,han2025computational}. These observations motivate sealed or covered equilibration experiments with post-run chemical analysis rather than assuming that the weighed composition is retained.

No published quaternary BaO--Y$_2$O$_3$--ZnO--SiO$_2$--O phase diagram was found in the vetted corpus. The appropriate conclusion is not that the target is unstable, but that its phase field and invariant reactions remain unmeasured. A minimal data package would combine isothermal equilibration at several temperatures, rapid quenching, EPMA phase compositions, powder XRD, and a thermodynamic assessment constrained by the binary and ternary edges \cite{shevchenko2021integrated,walters2026constructing,derensy2026phase}. The resulting map could then test whether a nominal BYZSO composition lies in a single-phase field, a tie triangle, or a liquid-plus-crystal region.

